{% extends "quarterly_deep_dive/llm_prompts/base_prompt.j2" %}

{% set output_format_description = "a brief, objective observation (2-3 sentences) focused solely on the primary trend or key finding from the 'Top Products by CVE Criticality' chart data. No interpretation or recommendations." %}

{% block task_instructions %}
The chart titled '{{ data_context_payload.chart_caption | default('Top Products by CVE Criticality') }}' (e.g., a bar chart) displays products ranked by the number or proportion of critical and high severity CVEs affecting them.
Examine the provided data summary for this chart.
Identify and describe the most significant observation. For example:
- Which product has the highest number of critical CVEs?
- Are there a few products that stand out with significantly more high-severity CVEs than others?
- How does the distribution of critical CVEs look across the top-listed products?
Focus only on what the data directly indicates about product criticality based on CVE counts and severities.
{% endblock task_instructions %}

{% block data_context %}
Chart ID: {{ data_context_payload.chart_id | default('top_products_by_criticality_chart') }}
Chart Caption: {{ data_context_payload.chart_caption | default('Figure 12. Top Products by CVE Criticality.') }}

Data Summary:
{{ data_context_payload.chart_data_summary | default("Data not available.") }}
Note: If percentages do not sum to 100%, this may be due to some CVEs lacking an assigned value (i.e., missing or NaN values were excluded from the calculation).
{% endblock data_context %}
